<section>
  <h2>Who this is for</h2>
  <p>Three jobs where a photo can carry too much.</p>
  <h3>eBay sellers</h3>
  <p>
    A listing photo with GPS in it tells buyers where the item is stored. Before you upload, run the
    picture through this metadata remover and keep the report with your records.
  </p>
  <h3>Etsy sellers</h3>
  <p>
    Product photos shot in a home studio carry the same device and location metadata as any phone
    picture. Removing it before listing keeps your workshop's location out of the public file.
  </p>
  <h3>Property listings</h3>
  <p>
    Rental and sale photos can expose more than the address you meant to publish, including interior
    shots tied to a device. Clean the files first, and use the
    <a href={LINKS.home.href}>metadata remover</a> report to confirm the fields are gone.
  </p>
</section>
